{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he looked, and behold, a well in the field</b> — His mother said to him: Just as I am beautiful of form and I happened to be at the well, so shall it be for you with my brother's daughters — if you see that she is like my form, she is your destined match:" "<b>Behold, a well in the field</b> — an allusion to the well that Israel had in the wilderness:" "<b>Three flocks</b> — in gematria this is Aaron and Moses and Miriam:" "<b>For from that well</b> — in gematria Moses:" "<b>And the stone</b> — two times in the parashah, after the manner of two stone tablets. Seven times \"well\" in the parashah, corresponding to the seven days of the Festival on which water libations are poured, and corresponding to the seven [people] who read from the Torah on Sabbath. Five of them [are] \"at the mouth of the well,\" corresponding to the five who read on a Festival, and three of them [are] \"above the mouth of the well,\" corresponding to the three who read on a weekday:"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:21.827437388Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}